{
  "description": "Monte Carlo statistics of terminal P&L and inventory. ce_mc is the sample CARA certainty equivalent (unreliable when gamma*std_pnl > 2); ce_exact is the exact value of the same quoting rule under an inventory limit of q_max_exact.",
  "params": {
    "s0": 100.0,
    "T": 1.0,
    "sigma": 2.0,
    "A": 140.0,
    "k": 1.5,
    "q0": 0,
    "dt": 0.005,
    "n_steps": 200,
    "n_paths": 100000,
    "seed": 2008,
    "q_max_exact": 30,
    "fixed_half_spread": 0.6666666666666666,
    "rng": "numpy default_rng (PCG64)"
  },
  "discretisation": [
    "each step: quotes from (T - t, q) before any fill",
    "at most one bid fill and one ask fill per step, independent, each with probability min(1, A*exp(-k*delta)*dt)",
    "bid fill: q += 1, cash -= s - delta_b; ask fill: q -= 1, cash += s + delta_a",
    "then the mid moves by sigma*sqrt(dt)*N(0,1)",
    "inventory and symmetric: spread = gamma*sigma^2*(T-t) + (2/gamma)*ln(1+gamma/k), centred on r = s - q*gamma*sigma^2*(T-t) and on s respectively; no inventory limit",
    "exact: GLFT optimal quotes with limit q_max_exact, table step = dt; fixed: half-spread 1/k",
    "pnl = cash_T + q_T * s_T; mean_spread = average of delta_a + delta_b over steps and paths"
  ],
